  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This preprint was later published in a peer-reviewed venue and already shows one documented downstream reuse in Europe PMC, indicating that the work has begun to circulate beyond its original posting. The available record is still early: OpenAlex shows no citations yet, so the strongest evidence at this stage comes from publication and reuse rather than citation accumulation.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Chromatin profiling for everyone: FFPE-CUTAC for the theory and practice of modern molecular biology presents both a methodological advance and a teaching-oriented research experience. The abstract shows that the authors developed a laboratory genomics course with Fred Hutch internship programs, using a new method designed to work with readily available fixed tissue sections on glass slides and to introduce students to modern molecular biology and bioinformatics.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The most tangible impact signal in the record is reuse: Europe PMC already registers one downstream article mention, suggesting that the work has been incorporated into later biomedical literature. That kind of reuse is an early sign of visibility and relevance, especially for a methods paper, because it indicates that other researchers are encountering and referencing the work in subsequent scholarly contexts.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The publication trajectory also matters here. The work began as a bioRxiv preprint and was later published in a peer-reviewed article, which extends its reach and suggests that the underlying method and educational framing were considered sufficiently robust for formal publication. OpenAIRE also shows two open instances for the work, consistent with broad accessibility to readers.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At the same time, the broader uptake record is still sparse. OpenAlex reports zero citations, and the available social and public-discourse indicators do not show additional tracked attention. For now, the narrative is therefore one of emerging scholarly circulation, with the clearest evidence centered on publication, open availability, and at least one documented reuse rather than on citation volume.</p>",
